    id: 'lsat-logic-game-festival-lineup',
    format: 'logic-game',
    publishedDate: '2026-06-27',
    publishedAt: '2026-06-27T19:44:58Z',
    title: 'LSAT Logic Games: A Festival Lineup',
    category: 'Logic Games',
    type: 'other',
    tags: ['other'],
    timeLimit: 600,
    blurb: "The LSAT's Analytical Reasoning section, better known as Logic Games, was retired in 2024 after a 42-year run. Here is an original game built in that exact format: one setup, five rules, seven questions. Read carefully and deduce.",
    source: { label: 'Original puzzle, built in the retired LSAT Analytical Reasoning (Logic Games) format' },
    setup: 'A music festival schedules exactly seven bands, F, G, H, J, K, L, and M, to perform one band at a time in seven consecutive slots numbered 1 through 7 (slot 1 is first, slot 7 is last). Each band performs exactly once. The schedule must meet all of the following conditions:',
    rules: [
      'F performs at some time before H.',
      'H performs at some time before G.',
      'G performs at some time before J.',
      'K performs in the slot immediately before the slot in which L performs.',
      'M performs either first or last.',
    ],
    questions: [
      {
        q: 'Which one of the following could be the order in which the bands perform, from slot 1 to slot 7?',
        choices: [
          'H, F, K, L, G, J, M',
          'F, H, K, L, G, J, M',
          'F, G, H, J, K, L, M',
          'M, F, H, G, J, L, K',
          'F, H, K, L, G, M, J',
        ],
        correct: 1,
        note: 'Each wrong choice breaks exactly one rule. H, F, ... puts H before F. F, G, H, ... puts G before H. M, F, H, G, J, L, K splits K from the slot just before L. F, H, K, L, G, M, J puts M in slot 6 rather than first or last. Only F, H, K, L, G, J, M obeys all five rules.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Which one of the following must be true?',
        choices: [
          'F performs first.',
          'J performs seventh.',
          'H performs third.',
          'G performs before J.',
          'K performs before F.',
        ],
        correct: 3,
        note: 'The chain F before H, H before G, G before J fixes G ahead of J in every valid schedule, so "G performs before J" must be true. F need not be first (M can open the show), J need not be last, and H and K can sit in several positions.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Which one of the following could be true?',
        choices: [
          'K performs sixth.',
          'F performs fifth.',
          'M performs fourth.',
          'J performs second.',
          'H performs first.',
        ],
        correct: 0,
        note: 'F can never be later than slot 4, M sits only in slot 1 or 7, J is never earlier than slot 4, and H is never first, so those four are impossible. K can perform sixth, for example M, F, H, G, J, K, L.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Which one of the following CANNOT be true?',
        choices: [
          'F performs second.',
          'G performs fourth.',
          'H performs sixth.',
          'L performs seventh.',
          'K performs after J.',
        ],
        correct: 2,
        note: 'F, then H, then G, then J all have bands that must follow them, which squeezes H no later than slot 5. So H sixth is impossible. Each of the other four can occur in some valid schedule.',
      },
      {
        q: 'If L performs fifth, then which one of the following must be true?',
        choices: [
          'M performs first.',
          'K performs fourth.',
          'J performs sixth.',
          'G performs third.',
          'F performs first.',
        ],
        correct: 1,
        note: 'K must sit in the slot immediately before L, so if L is fifth, K is fourth. That holds in both schedules that allow L fifth (F, H, G, K, L, J, M and M, F, H, K, L, G, J). Nothing else is forced: M, J, G, and F all vary between the two.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Which one of the following is a complete and accurate list of the slots in which H could perform?',
        choices: [
          '2, 3',
          '3, 4, 5',
          '2, 3, 4',
          '2, 3, 4, 5',
          '2, 3, 4, 5, 6',
        ],
        correct: 3,
        note: 'H must come after F and before both G and J, which keeps it between slot 2 and slot 5. It reaches slot 2 (for example F, H, K, L, G, J, M) and slot 5 (for example M, F, K, L, H, G, J), and every slot in between, so 2 through 5 is the complete range.',
      },
      {
        q: 'If H performs second, then which one of the following must be true?',
        choices: [
          'F performs first.',
          'G performs third.',
          'M performs first.',
          'J performs fourth.',
          'K performs fifth.',
        ],
        correct: 0,
        note: 'F has to perform before H, and if H is second the only slot left ahead of it is slot 1, so F performs first. The rest of the lineup can still be arranged in more than one way.',
      },
    ],
